# CI budgets II (docs/steps/ci-budgets-2/answered.md): a Windows session's
# open made cheaper at its cause, and the tests that run it made cheaper.

# --------------------------------------- the walk's look at a name, on Windows

[break] walk-takes-a-reparse-point-for-a-plain-name
rule: On Windows the walk takes a name for no link from its attributes only when they show no reparse point; a reparse point (a link, a junction) is looked at by `symlink_metadata`, which tells a link by its tag, and is followed by the walk itself.
file: crates/cineris-base/src/path/resolve.rs
in: is_link
find: Ok(attributes) if !attributes.is_reparse_point() => return Ok(false),
replace: Ok(_) => return Ok(false),
os: windows
caught-by:
    cineris-base path::resolve::tests::on_windows_the_walks_look_at_a_name_is_the_standard_librarys
    cineris-base::it paths_windows::a_link_to_a_network_share_is_refused_without_following_it

[break] walk-reads-a-directory-from-the-wrong-attribute
rule: On Windows a name with no reparse point is a directory when its attributes say so.
file: crates/cineris-base/src/path/resolve.rs
in: is_dir
find: return attributes.is_directory();
replace: return !attributes.is_directory();
os: windows
caught-by:
    cineris-base::it paths::the_workspace_must_be_an_existing_directory
    cineris-base::it paths::a_trailing_separator_names_a_directory

[break] attributes-never-a-reparse-point
rule: A name's attributes say it is a reparse point when Windows sets the bit: a link's own attributes, read without following it.
file: crates/cineris-base/src/private/windows.rs
in: is_reparse_point
find: self.0 & FILE_ATTRIBUTE_REPARSE_POINT != 0
replace: false
os: windows
caught-by:
    cineris-base private::windows::tests::a_names_attributes_say_whether_it_is_a_directory_or_a_reparse_point
    cineris-base path::resolve::tests::on_windows_the_walks_look_at_a_name_is_the_standard_librarys

[break] walk-takes-every-reparse-point-for-a-link
rule: A reparse point that is no link (a Unix domain socket's file, a cloud placeholder, a deduplicated file) is a plain name to the walk, as the standard library reads its tag: only its attributes' bit is not enough.
file: crates/cineris-base/src/path/resolve.rs
in: is_link
find: Ok(attributes) if !attributes.is_reparse_point() => return Ok(false),
replace: Ok(attributes) => return Ok(attributes.is_reparse_point()),
os: windows
caught-by:
    cineris-base::it paths_windows::sys_a_reparse_point_that_is_no_link_is_a_plain_name

[break] attributes-read-of-a-share
rule: A name's attributes are read only on one of the machine's own fixed disks: on a share they may be what the network client kept from an earlier look.
file: crates/cineris-base/src/private/windows.rs
in: on_a_fixed_disk
find: let rest = wide.strip_prefix(verbatim.as_slice()).unwrap_or(&wide);
replace: let rest = wide.strip_prefix(verbatim.as_slice()).unwrap_or(&wide); if rest.starts_with(&[92, 92]) || rest.starts_with(&[85, 78, 67]) { return true; }
os: windows
caught-by:
    cineris-base private::windows::tests::only_a_path_on_a_fixed_disk_has_its_attributes_read

[break] private-folder-taken-from-the-wrong-attribute
rule: On Windows `private::create_dir_all` takes a name with no reparse point for a folder that exists only when its attributes say it is a directory; a file there is refused.
file: crates/cineris-base/src/private/mod.rs
in: create_dir_all
find: if attributes.is_directory() {
replace: if !attributes.is_directory() {
os: windows
caught-by:
    cineris-base::it private::missing_directories_are_created_private_and_existing_ones_are_left_alone
    cineris-base::it private::a_file_on_the_way_is_an_error

# ------------------------------------------- a test's directories on a runner

[break] scratch-kept-on-a-desk
rule: On a desk, and a runner whose disk is kept, a test's directory is removed when the test ends.
file: crates/cineris-testkit/src/scratch.rs
in: drop
find: if !std::thread::panicking() && self.removed_at_end {
replace: if !std::thread::panicking() && !self.removed_at_end {
caught-by:
    cineris-testkit scratch::tests::it_is_removed_when_the_test_ends_read_only_files_included

[break] scratch-removed-on-a-hosted-runner
rule: On a GitHub-hosted runner, whose disk goes with the job, a test's directory is left when the test ends.
file: crates/cineris-testkit/src/scratch.rs
in: under_on
find: removed_at_end: !thrown_away
replace: removed_at_end: true
caught-by:
    cineris-testkit scratch::tests::on_a_runner_whose_disk_is_thrown_away_it_is_left_and_an_earlier_one_moved_aside

[break] scratch-leftover-removed-on-a-hosted-runner
rule: On a GitHub-hosted runner what an earlier run left is moved aside in one rename, not removed.
file: crates/cineris-testkit/src/scratch.rs
in: under_on
find: if dir.exists() && !(thrown_away && move_aside(&dir)) {
replace: if dir.exists() {
caught-by:
    cineris-testkit scratch::tests::on_a_runner_whose_disk_is_thrown_away_it_is_left_and_an_earlier_one_moved_aside

[break] scratch-hosted-runner-not-told
rule: A test's directories are left only on a runner that says it is GitHub-hosted.
file: crates/cineris-testkit/src/scratch.rs
in: says_leave
find: runner == "github-hosted"
replace: runner == "self-hosted"
caught-by:
    cineris-testkit scratch::tests::only_the_jobs_own_runs_on_a_github_hosted_runner_leave_their_directories

[break] scratch-left-by-a-run-not-told-to
rule: A test's directories are left only in a run told to leave them: the test job's own, not a stress run's or a break's, which repeat the tests and would fill the runner's disk.
file: crates/cineris-testkit/src/scratch.rs
in: says_leave
find: keep.is_some_and(|keep| keep == "1") && runner
replace: runner
caught-by:
    cineris-testkit scratch::tests::only_the_jobs_own_runs_on_a_github_hosted_runner_leave_their_directories

